DTSTAMP:20260822T232237Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260630
SUMMARY:[Federal Maine-Related] MULTIPLE APPOINTMENTS TO PANEL OF CHAPTER 
 7 TRUSTEES
DESCRIPTION:Tuesday\, June 30\, 2026\nThe United States Trustee seeks resu
 mes from persons wishing to be considered for\nappointment to the panel of
  trustees who administer cases filed under chapter 7 of title 11 of the\nU
 nited States Code (Bankruptcy Code). The appointments are for cases filed 
 in the United\nStates Bankruptcy Court for the Districts of Massachusetts\
 , New Hampshire\, and Rhode Island.\nChapter 7 trustees receive compensati
 on and reimbursement for expenses under 11 U.S.C. §§\n326 and 330. Altho
 ugh trustees are not federal employees\, appointments are made consistent\
 nwith federal Equal Opportunity policies\, which prohibit discrimination i
 n employment. For\nadditional information\, qualification requirements\, a
 nd application procedures go to\nhttp://www.justice.gov/ust/eo/private_tru
 stee/vacancies/7ad.htm\nhttps://www.meb.uscourts.gov/news/multiple-appoint
 ments-panel-chapter-7-trustees
URL:https://www.meb.uscourts.gov/news/multiple-appointments-panel-chapter-
 7-trustees
CATEGORIES:Federal Maine-Related
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
